703
00:33:06,480 --> 00:33:08,360
Right there on the green.

704
00:33:08,460 --> 00:33:09,000
Go ahead.

705
00:33:09,000 --> 00:33:09,520
Go ahead.

706
00:33:09,520 --> 00:33:09,820
Secretary.

707
00:33:09,860 --> 00:33:10,620
Yes, sir.

708
00:33:11,520 --> 00:33:16,660
Minister Secretary, does the President intend to press Beijing on its Taiwan policy when

709
00:33:16,700 --> 00:33:18,220
he visits China next week?

710
00:33:18,220 --> 00:33:20,180
I'm sure Taiwan will be a topic of conversation.

711
00:33:20,180 --> 00:33:21,020
It always is.

712
00:33:21,160 --> 00:33:25,300
As you know, we understand the Chinese understand our position on that topic.

713
00:33:25,300 --> 00:33:26,360
We understand theirs.

714
00:33:26,580 --> 00:33:31,280
And I think both parties, without getting ahead of myself of what will happen in the talks,

715
00:33:31,460 --> 00:33:33,220
but I think both countries understand.

716
00:33:33,580 --> 00:33:38,260
that it is neither one of our interests to see anything destabilize happen in that part of the world.

717
00:33:38,260 --> 00:33:43,840
We don't need any destabilizing events to occur with regards to Taiwan or anywhere in the Indo-Pacific.

718
00:33:43,880 --> 00:33:47,140
And I think that's to the mutual benefit of both the United States and the Chinese.

719
00:33:48,880 --> 00:33:49,700
Secretary of State.

720
00:33:49,700 --> 00:33:52,420
Hey, Kara Kastanova from LZLTV, thank you.

721
00:33:52,440 --> 00:33:55,560
for taking my question today. How does the State Department...

722
00:33:55,600 --> 00:33:59,620
What happened? Why is everybody giggling? What happened? Oh, I'm sorry.

723
00:33:59,680 --> 00:34:02,280
Are they not me and you? No, they're not me and you. Oh, okay.

724
00:34:02,580 --> 00:34:07,680
I don't think they are. I hope not. But I'm here on Lindell TV and nice to ask you a question today, sir.

725
00:34:07,880 --> 00:34:11,720
How does the State Department interpret the President's recent remarks when he said, quote,

726
00:34:12,040 --> 00:34:16,460
the Iranian people need to have guns, and I think they are getting some guns, end quote. What did he

727
00:34:16,620 --> 00:34:21,240
mean and do those comments relate to any ongoing or potential U.S. actions like supplying those

728
00:34:21,380 --> 00:34:21,500
weapons?

729
00:34:21,500 --> 00:34:23,800
Well, I think it goes back to the question I was asked a moment ago.

730
00:34:23,800 --> 00:34:27,560
I think the president thinks it's heartbreaking that the Iranian people are abused by this

731
00:34:27,700 --> 00:34:28,880
regime the way they are.

732
00:34:28,880 --> 00:34:30,320
In the end, I mean, this regime is not...

733
00:34:30,420 --> 00:34:34,140
Guys, I know I've said this, I think I said this in my hearing before the Senate when I

734
00:34:34,140 --> 00:34:34,680
got confirmed.

735
00:34:35,180 --> 00:34:38,300
I don't know of any country in the world where there's a bigger difference between the

736
00:34:39,080 --> 00:34:40,260
people and the people who run the country.

737
00:34:40,660 --> 00:34:43,280
This country is run by radical Shia clerics.

738
00:34:43,620 --> 00:34:46,280
And that's not what Iran and the Iranian people are.

739
00:34:46,280 --> 00:34:48,920
Now, they may be Shia, but they're not radicals and they're not clerics

740
00:34:49,140 --> 00:34:51,180
and they just want a normal life and a regular life

741
00:34:51,560 --> 00:34:55,000
in many ways a very cosmopolitan country with an incredible history,

742
00:34:55,360 --> 00:34:57,760
incredible history and incredible legacy and the like.

743
00:34:57,980 --> 00:35:00,880
So there's this huge divide between the people of Iran

744
00:35:01,180 --> 00:35:02,320
whom we sympathize with.

745
00:35:02,340 --> 00:35:05,360
and who the president sympathizes with, because they're the ones suffering.

746
00:35:05,380 --> 00:35:07,040
Look, the world is a victim of Iran, okay?

747
00:35:07,180 --> 00:35:09,100
The world is a victim of Iran because they're terrorists,

748
00:35:09,160 --> 00:35:11,100
because of what they're doing now in the Straits.

749
00:35:11,240 --> 00:35:13,980
But the people of Iran are daily victims of the regime,

750
00:35:13,980 --> 00:35:16,200
and the president has deep sympathy for what they're going through.

751
00:35:16,500 --> 00:35:19,380
And I think he's just expressing that sympathy and that frustration

752
00:35:19,780 --> 00:35:22,560
that they don't have the ability to do more to get rid of this regime

753
00:35:23,040 --> 00:35:26,600
that has crushed this country and isolated it from the world,

754
00:35:26,600 --> 00:35:28,340
which is a country that shouldn't be isolated from the world,

755
00:35:28,340 --> 00:35:29,600
because its people are phenomenal.

756
00:35:29,780 --> 00:35:29,780
Right.

757
00:35:29,860 --> 00:35:30,560
All right.

758
00:35:33,820 --> 00:35:36,040
I wish I had like a dice, go ahead.

759
00:35:36,060 --> 00:35:39,840
No, no, no, no, no, no, no, right there, because I'm going to Italy.

760
00:35:39,900 --> 00:35:40,020
.

761
00:35:40,440 --> 00:35:44,900
He's Italian. I know him, he used to cover Capitol Hill.

762
00:35:44,900 --> 00:35:45,740
You're Italian, right?

763
00:35:45,740 --> 00:35:46,540
For many years.

764
00:35:46,560 --> 00:35:47,700
For many years.

765
00:35:47,700 --> 00:35:47,880
Okay.

766
00:35:47,880 --> 00:35:49,920
Daniela Capatangelo, thank you, Mr. Secretary.

767
00:35:49,940 --> 00:35:51,620
So I have two short questions for you.

768
00:35:51,740 --> 00:35:53,680
Oh, the damn two questions.

769
00:35:53,680 --> 00:35:59,800
First, as you head to the Vatican and Italy, how do you view the Pope's global role

770
00:35:59,940 --> 00:36:01,600
amid current geopolitical shift?

771
00:36:02,140 --> 00:36:04,800
And what are your objectives in Italy?

772
00:36:04,900 --> 00:36:07,760
Is this trip tied to recent remarks by the president,

773
00:36:07,820 --> 00:36:10,560
suggesting Italy has not been supporter as expected?

774
00:36:10,700 --> 00:36:14,000
And the second one is about the Headsbourne Line Lebanon.

775
00:36:14,120 --> 00:36:16,880
On a recent interview on Fox News,

776
00:36:16,880 --> 00:36:19,840
you raised some concern about stronger vetting

777
00:36:19,920 --> 00:36:21,240
within the Lebanese armed forces.

778
00:36:21,440 --> 00:36:25,540
Can you, what do you make, can you elaborate a little bit?

779
00:36:25,560 --> 00:36:27,200
I've answered the first one about the Vatican.

780
00:36:27,320 --> 00:36:30,780
Look, I mean, the Pope is obviously the vicar of Christ, is a Roman Catholic, you know,

781
00:36:31,180 --> 00:36:39,280
but he's also the head of a nation state for a lot, you know, and it's an organization that has a presence in over 100-something countries around the world.

782
00:36:39,500 --> 00:36:43,220
And we engage with the Vatican quite a bit because they're present in many different places.

783
00:36:43,220 --> 00:36:44,620
I've already outlined to you two examples.

784
00:36:45,020 --> 00:36:48,280
We worked with the Catholic Church on the distribution of humanitarian aid in Cuba.

785
00:36:48,540 --> 00:36:52,980
We share with the Catholic Church a concern about the destruction of religious liberty,

786
00:36:52,980 --> 00:36:58,340
the persecution of Christian minorities, and also the challenges that are being faced by Christians in Africa

787
00:36:59,060 --> 00:37:00,920
where the Pope just recently visited.

788
00:37:00,980 --> 00:37:05,340
So we have a lot to talk about with them, and I engage with them quite a bit on that front.

789
00:37:05,660 --> 00:37:06,800
So the trip is...

790
00:37:07,600 --> 00:37:11,040
really not tied to anything other than the fact that it would be normal for us to engage with them.

791
00:37:11,040 --> 00:37:13,060
And other Secretary of State have done that in the past.

792
00:37:13,380 --> 00:37:16,460
On the second point about Lebanon, also a question that was asked earlier.

793
00:37:17,220 --> 00:37:18,560
What was the Italian for?

794
00:37:18,560 --> 00:37:20,740
About the expectation that the president...

795
00:37:20,840 --> 00:37:22,540
Oh, no, look, I mean, the Italians have been involved

796
00:37:22,540 --> 00:37:24,540
for quite a, for some time in training the police

797
00:37:24,620 --> 00:37:25,740
and in training their forces,

798
00:37:25,740 --> 00:37:27,300
so we'd love to hear their input on it.

799
00:37:27,640 --> 00:37:29,920
And in the way, look, we welcome everybody's help eventually.

800
00:37:30,080 --> 00:37:31,300
What has to happen in Lebanon,

801
00:37:31,300 --> 00:37:32,420
what everybody wants to see,

802
00:37:32,720 --> 00:37:33,920
is that you have a Lebanese government

803
00:37:34,400 --> 00:37:36,700
with the capability to go after Hezbollah

804
00:37:36,820 --> 00:37:38,160
and take the Hezbollah apart.

805
00:37:38,340 --> 00:37:39,280
There shouldn't be...

806
00:37:39,640 --> 00:37:42,480
Like, there shouldn't be a Hezbollah and a government.

807
00:37:42,620 --> 00:37:43,340
There should be a government.

808
00:37:43,420 --> 00:37:44,840
Everyone should fold underneath it.

809
00:37:44,840 --> 00:37:47,320
And if we do that, then there will be peace between Israel and Lebanon.

810
00:37:47,500 --> 00:37:51,220
But we have to build the capacity of the Lebanese to do it.

811
00:37:51,300 --> 00:37:53,320
And I think Italy could be helpful in that in that regard.

812
00:37:53,640 --> 00:37:54,900
All right.

813
00:37:56,020 --> 00:37:57,440
Did I call on you already?

814
00:37:57,440 --> 00:37:58,640
You already got a question?

815
00:37:58,840 --> 00:37:59,300
In the green?

816
00:37:59,300 --> 00:37:59,720
Yes.

817
00:38:00,280 --> 00:38:01,980
Did I call on you already?

818
00:38:02,160 --> 00:38:02,260
No.

819
00:38:02,260 --> 00:38:03,260
Okay, all right.

820
00:38:03,500 --> 00:38:03,980
Go ahead.

821
00:38:03,980 --> 00:38:06,760
You mentioned the UN resolution that you announced today.

822
00:38:06,840 --> 00:38:09,420
Can you talk about what the goal is with that resolution?

823
00:38:09,420 --> 00:38:13,280
And there was a similar one last month that was vetoed by China and Russia.

824
00:38:13,440 --> 00:38:15,180
You spoke to the Russian foreign minister.

825
00:38:15,180 --> 00:38:18,040
Do you have an assurance that Russia will be on board with this now?

826
00:38:18,040 --> 00:38:18,700
Well, we don't know.

827
00:38:18,700 --> 00:38:19,160
I don't know.

828
00:38:19,160 --> 00:38:21,260
Yeah, look, I mean, everyone wouldn't want to see this vetoed again.

829
00:38:21,300 --> 00:38:23,460
And then we've made some slight adjustments to the language.

830
00:38:23,540 --> 00:38:25,060
I don't know if it'll avoid a veto or not.

831
00:38:25,060 --> 00:38:26,560
But the language isn't very complicated.

832
00:38:26,940 --> 00:38:26,940
Yeah.

833
00:38:26,760 --> 00:38:31,340
And I think it's a real test for the UN, right, as a function, as something that functions

834
00:38:31,400 --> 00:38:33,920
to, that can solve global problems.

835
00:38:34,500 --> 00:38:35,680
What is the purpose of the UN?

836
00:38:35,680 --> 00:38:39,480
The UN was supposed to be a place where you could peacefully resolve global conflict.

837
00:38:39,860 --> 00:38:43,700
Right now you have a country who is unlawfully, criminally and illegally.

838
00:38:44,000 --> 00:38:50,020
taking possession of an international waterway and blowing up commercial vessels and putting mines in the water.

839
00:38:50,020 --> 00:38:59,100
I don't know if people appreciate how outrageous this is, how unacceptable it is that any country would fire and try to sink commercial vessels or put mines in the water.

840
00:38:59,100 --> 00:39:00,160
Both of these things are illegal.

841
00:39:00,500 --> 00:39:01,800
And so we're going to take it to the UN.

842
00:39:01,820 --> 00:39:08,680
And we're going to give it another chance to be a forum in which we're not even asking people to like commit troops to the region and help blow up the Iranian boats.

843
00:39:08,960 --> 00:39:19,300
All we're asking them to do is to condemn it, to call on Iran, to stop blowing ships, to remove these mines, and to allow humanitarian relief to come through because there's humanitarian aid that's trapped.

844
00:39:19,500 --> 00:39:19,720
That's it.

845
00:39:19,900 --> 00:39:21,360
There's a very modest request.

846
00:39:21,740 --> 00:39:24,240
And if you're telling me that the international community...

847
00:39:24,280 --> 00:39:28,780
And hundreds of countries cannot rally behind that, then I don't know what the utility of

848
00:39:28,860 --> 00:39:32,240
the UN system is, if it can't even solve something as straightforward as that.

849
00:39:32,240 --> 00:39:35,860
And I think to both the Chinese and the Russians, I would argue and have argued that it is

850
00:39:35,860 --> 00:39:40,440
in their interest for that resolution to pass and for pressure to be brought on Iran,

851
00:39:40,520 --> 00:39:43,800
because it is in their interest not to see international waterways, including the Straits

852
00:39:43,800 --> 00:39:49,180
of Hormuz, be closed down and cause economic chaos to dozens and dozens of countries around

853
00:39:49,180 --> 00:39:49,840
the world.

854
00:39:52,100 --> 00:39:54,420
Back row, yellow tie.

855
00:39:54,420 --> 00:39:56,100
Thank you.

856
00:39:56,100 --> 00:39:58,540
Secretary, tell me where it's CBN news?

857
00:39:58,580 --> 00:40:01,740
You've had a deep faith for God and country.

858
00:40:02,720 --> 00:40:04,840
At the end of the day, with all that you've been involved in,

859
00:40:04,940 --> 00:40:05,340
keep going.

860
00:40:05,340 --> 00:40:06,780
You've been extremely busy.

861
00:40:06,860 --> 00:40:07,680
Go ahead, I'm sorry.

862
00:40:07,680 --> 00:40:13,500
As we all know, I got to ask you, what is your hope for America at a time such as this?

863
00:40:13,940 --> 00:40:15,700
My hope for America?

864
00:40:15,960 --> 00:40:18,040
And how do you personally deal with that?

865
00:40:18,220 --> 00:40:20,380
Yeah, look, I mean, my hope for America is what it's always been.

866
00:40:20,380 --> 00:40:22,140
I think it's the hope I hope we all share.

867
00:40:22,140 --> 00:40:25,800
We want it to continue to be the place where anyone from anywhere can achieve anything.

868
00:40:26,220 --> 00:40:30,620
Where you're not limited by the circumstances of your birth, by the color of your skin, by your ethnicity,

869
00:40:30,660 --> 00:40:35,280
but frankly, it's a place where you are able to overcome challenges and achieve your full potential.

870
00:40:35,420 --> 00:40:39,720
I think that should be the goal of every country in the world, frankly, but I think in the U.S., we're not perfect.

871
00:40:39,720 --> 00:40:42,740
Our history is not one of perfection, but it's still better than anybody else's history.

872
00:40:42,780 --> 00:40:45,880
history, and ours is a story of perpetual improvement.

873
00:40:45,980 --> 00:40:50,440
Each generation has left the next generation of Americans freer, more prosperous, safer,

874
00:40:50,440 --> 00:40:51,860
and that is our goal as well.

875
00:40:51,860 --> 00:40:56,240
But it is a unique and exceptional country, and as we come upon this 250-year anniversary,

876
00:40:56,240 --> 00:40:58,680
I think we have a lot to learn and be proud of in our history.

877
00:40:58,940 --> 00:41:03,420
It is one of perpetual and continuous improvement where each generation has done its part to

878
00:41:03,520 --> 00:41:06,880
bring us closer to fulfilling the vision that the founders of this country had upon its

879
00:41:07,240 --> 00:41:07,380
founding.

880
00:41:07,480 --> 00:41:08,860
So thank you.

881
00:41:09,080 --> 00:41:09,440
All right.

882
00:41:10,060 --> 00:41:12,980
I have time for two more questions.

883
00:41:16,340 --> 00:41:19,540
All right, right there in the pink.

884
00:41:19,640 --> 00:41:20,780
No, no, no, you right there.

885
00:41:20,860 --> 00:41:22,820
No, that lady, no, the one right next to you in the pink.

886
00:41:23,260 --> 00:41:24,600
No, no, no, no, the pink.

887
00:41:24,600 --> 00:41:26,160
I'm sorry, but I pointed at her.

888
00:41:26,480 --> 00:41:27,600
I need to get a laser pointer.

889
00:41:27,740 --> 00:41:28,460
Just go ahead.

890
00:41:28,900 --> 00:41:31,100
Now you in the pink jacket, the lady right there.

891
00:41:31,100 --> 00:41:31,560
Thank you.

892
00:41:31,920 --> 00:41:33,060
Thank you very much, Mr. Secretary.

893
00:41:33,060 --> 00:41:36,460
I have a question on Iran-China relations.

894
00:41:36,460 --> 00:41:36,860
Okay.

895
00:41:36,860 --> 00:41:40,640
What's your reaction to Iranian foreign minister visit to China?

896
00:41:40,640 --> 00:41:46,360
Also Beijing instructed its firms to ignore U.S. sanctions.

897
00:41:46,360 --> 00:41:47,540
Could you also address that?

898
00:41:47,600 --> 00:41:49,720
Well, I'll direct you to Treasury on that front.

899
00:41:49,720 --> 00:41:50,720
There are options that we have.

900
00:41:50,720 --> 00:41:53,240
If you ignore our sanctions, you're going to face secondary sanctions.

901
00:41:53,500 --> 00:41:56,440
And I don't have an announcement for you on that today, but we don't do these things,

902
00:41:56,440 --> 00:41:58,280
you know, for symbolic purposes.

903
00:41:58,460 --> 00:42:01,420
On the first point about the visit, it's fine.

904
00:42:01,460 --> 00:42:03,200
I hope the Chinese tell him what he needs to be told,

905
00:42:03,200 --> 00:42:05,020
and that is that what you are doing in the Straits

906
00:42:05,180 --> 00:42:07,000
is causing you to be globally isolated.

907
00:42:07,160 --> 00:42:08,260
You're the bad guy in this.

908
00:42:08,400 --> 00:42:10,300
You guys should not be blowing up ships.

909
00:42:10,320 --> 00:42:11,440
You should not be putting mines.

910
00:42:11,740 --> 00:42:12,460
You should not be...

911
00:42:12,780 --> 00:42:16,440
holding hostage, the global, trying to hold hostage, the global economy.

912
00:42:16,440 --> 00:42:19,500
I hope the Chinese bring, whether it's done privately, but I hope it's done directly,

913
00:42:19,500 --> 00:42:21,220
that that's the message they deliver to them.

914
00:42:21,240 --> 00:42:25,640
As I outlined earlier today, China is an export-driven economy.

915
00:42:25,680 --> 00:42:28,780
Okay, I'm not here to speak on behalf of what's in the best interest of China, but it's obvious.

916
00:42:29,100 --> 00:42:31,140
China is an export-driven economy.

917
00:42:31,220 --> 00:42:34,260
That means they depend on other countries to buy from them.

918
00:42:34,260 --> 00:42:36,640
Well, you can't buy from them if you can't ship it there,

919
00:42:36,660 --> 00:42:40,560
and you can't buy from them if your economy is being destroyed by what Iran is doing.

920
00:42:40,720 --> 00:42:45,240
So it is in China's interest that Iran stop closing the straits.

921
00:42:45,240 --> 00:42:46,740
It's harming China as well.

922
00:42:46,700 --> 00:42:48,260
The gentleman in the red tie.

923
00:42:48,320 --> 00:42:48,980
Right there.

924
00:42:49,180 --> 00:42:51,380
Thank you, Secretary.

925
00:42:52,720 --> 00:42:54,960
Yes, I'm sorry, what's your name?

926
00:42:54,960 --> 00:42:56,480
Liz Landers of PBS News Argus.

927
00:42:56,620 --> 00:42:59,100
Another question about the China-Iran relationship.

928
00:42:59,100 --> 00:43:04,860
You said at the beginning of your comments at the top that every single financial situation will be targeted.

929
00:43:05,100 --> 00:43:06,920
Does that include Chinese banks?

930
00:43:06,920 --> 00:43:07,620
Would the president sanction...

931
00:43:07,620 --> 00:43:08,820
We're going to enforce our sanctions.

932
00:43:08,820 --> 00:43:10,140
Chinese banks will bring us to Beijing.

933
00:43:10,160 --> 00:43:13,820
I don't have an announcement for you that will have to come from Treasury, but we have sanctions in place.

934
00:43:14,120 --> 00:43:17,600
And sanctions don't mean anything unless, you know, you're going to do something about them.

935
00:43:17,600 --> 00:43:18,700
So I think that's been clear.

936
00:43:19,060 --> 00:43:23,040
I think the, you know, the Treasury will follow up with any specific announcements.

937
00:43:23,420 --> 00:43:25,400
Suffice it to say we're serious about our sanctions.

938
00:43:25,880 --> 00:43:28,680
Then a cost needs to be imposed on Iran for what they are doing.

939
00:43:28,940 --> 00:43:34,900
Otherwise, if they get away with this guys, if they get away with being pulling this thing off without paying a price for it and backing down,

940
00:43:34,900 --> 00:43:39,160
